  "description": "The per-host member of a swarm of worker processes. One runs on each host: it subscribes to the swarm's coordinator before it does anything else, measures the host's memory and processor load behind an interface with implementations for Debian-based Linux, Windows and macOS, and starts Worker processes only while the host still has room for them - one at a time, re-measuring between each. It hands every Worker its configuration over a private pipe that stays open as a lifeline, notices when one exits, waits longer after one that failed immediately, and ends them all in an orderly way when the coordinator says the work is over. Pair it with CodeBrix.Swarm.Queen and CodeBrix.Swarm.Worker, and install all three at the same version.",
